    "eval_id": "eval_7157_002",
    "query": "Who must complete the annual risk assessment submission to the CPPA, and what specific legal declaration must be signed under penalty of perjury?",
    "target_section": "7157",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.25,
    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7157(b)(5) and \u00a7 7157(c), the submission must be made via cppa.ca.gov by an executive management team member directly responsible for risk-assessment compliance with sufficient knowledge and authority. The executive must electronically sign an attestation under penalty of perjury under California law declaring that the business conducted the required risk assessments and that the submitted information is true and correct.",
    "generated_answer": "Pursuant to the provided regulations, the requirements for submitting risk assessments are as follows:\n\n### Who Must Complete the Submission\nThe individual submitting the risk assessment information to the Agency must be a member of the business\u2019s **executive management team** who meets the following criteria (\u00a7 7157(c)):\n\n*   **Responsibility**: The individual must be directly responsible for the business\u2019s risk-assessment compliance.\n*   **Knowledge**: The individual must possess sufficient knowledge of the business\u2019s risk assessment to provide accurate information.\n*   **Authority**: The individual must have the authority to submit the risk assessment information to the Agency.\n\n### Required Legal Declaration\nThe submission must include an attestation, signed by the executive management team member, which includes the following statement under penalty of perjury (\u00a7 7157(b)(5)):\n\n> \u201cI attest that the business has conducted a risk assessment for the processing activities set forth in California Code of Regulations, Title 11, section 7150, subsection (b), during the time period covered by this submission, and that I meet the requirements of section 7157, subsection (c). Under penalty of perjury under the laws of the state of California, I hereby declare that the risk assessment information submitted is true and correct.\u201d",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9283,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is legally precise, complete, and fully aligned with the ground truth. It correctly identifies the required personnel (executive management team member with responsibility, knowledge, and authority) and provides the exact text of the required attestation under penalty of perjury as specified in the regulations.",
