    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7123(c)(16), the cybersecurity audit must evaluate retention schedules and proper disposal procedures for personal information no longer needed. Proper disposal must be accomplished by: (A) Shredding; (B) Erasing; or (C) Otherwise modifying the personal information in those records to render it unreadable or undecipherable through any means.",
    "generated_answer": "According to **\u00a7 7123(16)**, when personal information is no longer required to be retained, a business must ensure its proper disposal by utilizing one of the following methods:\n\n*   **(A) Shredding**\n*   **(B) Erasing**\n*   **(C) Otherwise modifying** the personal information in those records to make it unreadable or undecipherable through any means.\n\nAdditionally, businesses are required to maintain retention schedules to determine when personal information is no longer required to be retained **(\u00a7 7123(16))**.",
