    "eval_id": "eval_7124_003",
    "query": "What specific legal attestation statement and standard of perjury are required when submitting the \u00a7 7124 cybersecurity audit certification online?",
    "target_section": "7124",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.25,
    "key_term_recall": 0.4,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7124(d)(4), the submitter must electronically sign an attestation under penalty of perjury under California state law declaring that the information submitted is true and correct, that they meet \u00a7 7124(c) executive criteria, and that the business has not made any attempt to influence the auditor's decisions or assessments regarding the cybersecurity audit.",
    "generated_answer": "To submit the cybersecurity audit certification required under \u00a7 7124, a business must provide an electronically signed attestation that includes specific language and acknowledges the legal standard of perjury.\n\n### Required Attestation Statement\nPursuant to **\u00a7 7124(d)(4)**, the business must include an electronically signed attestation to the following statement:\n\n> \u201cI attest that I meet the requirements of California Code of Regulations, Title 11, section 7124, subsection (c), to submit this certification. Under penalty of perjury under the laws of the state of California, I hereby declare that the information contained within and submitted with this certification is true and correct and that the business has not made any attempt to influence the auditor\u2019s decisions or assessments regarding the cybersecurity audit.\u201d\n\n### Legal Standard and Requirements\n*   **Perjury Standard**: The submission must be made \"under penalty of perjury under the laws of the state of California\" (**\u00a7 7124(d)(4)**).\n*   **Signatory Qualifications**: Under **\u00a7 7124(c)**, the person signing the attestation must be a member of the business\u2019s executive management team who:\n    *   Is directly responsible for the business\u2019s cybersecurity-audit compliance;\n    *   Has sufficient knowledge of the business\u2019s cybersecurity audit to provide accurate information; and\n    *   Has the authority to submit the business\u2019s certification to the Agency.\n*   **Additional Submission Details**: The certification is submitted via the Agency\u2019s website at https://cppa.ca.gov/ and must also include the business\u2019s name, the point of contact\u2019s information (name, phone, email), a statement confirming the audit is complete, the time period covered by the audit (month and year), and the name, title, and date of the person submitting the certification (**\u00a7 7124(d)(1)\u2013(3), (5)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9011,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is exceptionally accurate and comprehensive. It not only addresses the specific requirements mentioned in the ground truth but provides the exact regulatory text of the attestation statement and clarifies the signatory qualifications, which adds significant value while remaining strictly aligned with the legal requirements of \u00a7 7124.",
