  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7123_005",
    "query": "What certification statement and auditor sign-off requirements must be included in a final CCPA cybersecurity audit report?",
    "target_section": "7123",
    "expected_route": "HYBRID_BOTH",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": false,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": false,
    "precision_at_k": 0.4,
    "key_term_recall": 0.8,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7123(e)(8), the cybersecurity audit report must include a statement signed and dated by the highest-ranking auditor certifying that they completed an independent review of the business's program and system, exercised objective and impartial judgment on all issues, and did not rely primarily on assertions or attestations by the business's management.",
    "generated_answer": "To comply with California privacy regulations regarding the final cybersecurity audit report, you must include two distinct types of documentation: an electronically signed certification for the Agency (submitted by the business) and an auditor-signed statement within the audit report itself.\n\n### 1. Business Certification to the Agency\nPer **\u00a7 7124**, when a business submits its certification to the Agency, the executive management member must include an electronically signed attestation stating the following:\n\n> \u201cI attest that I meet the requirements of California Code of Regulations, Title 11, section 7124, subsection (c), to submit this certification. Under penalty of perjury under the laws of the state of California, I hereby declare that the information contained within and submitted with this certification is true and correct and that the business has not made any attempt to influence the auditor\u2019s decisions or assessments regarding the cybersecurity audit.\u201d\n\n### 2. Auditor Sign-off Requirements\nPer **\u00a7 7123(e)(8)**, the cybersecurity audit report must include a statement signed and dated by the highest-ranking auditor that certifies the following:\n\n*   **Independent Review**: The auditor completed an independent review of the business\u2019s cybersecurity program and information system.\n*   **Objectivity**: The auditor exercised objective and impartial judgment on all issues within the scope of the cybersecurity audit.\n*   **Independence from Management**: The auditor did not rely primarily on assertions or attestations by the business\u2019s management.\n\n***\n\n**Additional Reporting Requirements:**\nIn addition to the specific sign-offs mentioned above, **\u00a7 7123(e)(7)** requires the report to identify the auditor\u2019s name, affiliation, and relevant qualifications to ensure transparency and accountability.",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.7887,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is legally precise, accurate, and provides more comprehensive context than the ground truth while remaining fully aligned with the specific requirements of \u00a7 7123(e)(8). It correctly identifies the auditor sign-off requirements and adds relevant, accurate context regarding the business certification and auditor identification requirements.",
