  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7152_007",
    "query": "What privacy-enhancing technologies (PETs) and technical safeguards are highlighted in \u00a7 7152(a)(6) for mitigating processing risks in a risk assessment?",
    "target_section": "7152",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.6667,
    "key_term_recall": 1.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7152(a)(6)(A)(i)\u2013(iv), recommended safeguards include technical controls (encryption, system segmentation, access controls), privacy-enhancing technologies (trusted execution environments, federated learning, homomorphic encryption, differential privacy), consulting external bias/privacy experts, and implementing ADMT anti-discrimination policies and training.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory text, \u00a7 7152 explicitly lists privacy-enhancing technologies (PETs) and technical safeguards that a business may consider for inclusion in its risk assessment to mitigate identified negative impacts on consumer privacy.\n\n### Privacy-Enhancing Technologies (PETs)\nUnder **\u00a7 7152(i)(ii)**, the regulation identifies the following examples of privacy-enhancing technologies:\n*   Trusted execution environments\n*   Federated learning\n*   Homomorphic encryption\n*   Differential privacy\n\n### Technical Safeguards\nUnder **\u00a7 7152(i)(i)**, the regulation lists the following examples of technical safeguards for information systems:\n*   Encryption\n*   Segmentation of information systems\n*   Physical and logical access controls\n*   Change management\n*   Network monitoring and defenses\n*   Data and integrity monitoring\n\nAdditionally, **\u00a7 7152(i)(iii)** and **(iv)** identify the following operational and procedural safeguards to mitigate privacy risks:\n*   **Consulting external parties**: Engaging with external experts to maintain current knowledge of emergent privacy risks and countermeasures.\n*   **Policies and Training**: Implementing policies, procedures, and training to ensure that Automated Decision-Making Technology (ADMT) functions for the intended business purpose and avoids unlawful discrimination based on protected characteristics.\n\n***Note on Scope:** While you requested information regarding \u00a7 7152(a)(6), the specific lists of technologies and safeguards above are detailed in the subsection labeled (i) through (iv) of \u00a7 7152. These items serve as the components for the \"safeguards\" requirement mandated in the risk assessment process.*",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8806,
    "llm_judge_score": 4.5,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is highly accurate and provides a more comprehensive list of safeguards than the ground truth, correctly identifying the specific subsections (i)-(iv) that contain these requirements. It correctly identifies the PETs and technical safeguards. The slight deduction is due to the candidate referencing \u00a7 7152(i) instead of the requested \u00a7 7152(a)(6); while the candidate correctly notes the discrepancy in their 'Note on Scope,' the regulation actually nests these requirements under \u00a7 7152(a)(6)(A)(i)-(iv). Despite this minor citation nuance, the content is legally precise and superior in detail.",
    "model_refusal": false,
