    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7123(c)(13), cybersecurity education and training must be provided to each employee, independent contractor, and personnel with system access at three specific points: (1) When their employment or contract begins; (2) Annually thereafter; and (3) Following a personal information security breach as described in Civil Code section 1798.150.",
    "generated_answer": "Pursuant to **\u00a7 7123(13)**, a business is required to provide cybersecurity education and training to each employee, independent contractor, and any other personnel to whom the business provides access to its information system. \n\nUnder this section, the three specific time points or events that trigger this training obligation are:\n\n*   **At the start of their engagement:** When the individual's employment or contract begins.\n*   **On a recurring basis:** Annually following the initial training.\n*   **Post-incident:** After the occurrence of a personal information security breach, as described in Civil Code section 1798.150.",
