    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7002(f), a business shall not collect categories of personal information other than those disclosed in its Notice at Collection. If it intends to collect additional categories or use data for incompatible additional purposes, it must provide a new Notice at Collection before collecting the data, and comply with all necessity and proportionality rules in \u00a7 7002(a)\u2013(e).",
    "generated_answer": "Under the provided regulatory context, if a business intends to collect additional categories of personal information not disclosed in its initial Notice at Collection, it must take the following step:\n\n*   **Provide a new Notice at Collection:** The business must provide a new Notice at Collection that discloses the additional categories of personal information being collected (\u00a7 7002(f)).\n\nFurthermore, the business must ensure that this additional collection and processing remains in compliance with the requirements set forth in **\u00a7 7002(a) \u2013 (e)**, which include:\n\n*   **Reasonable Necessity and Proportionality:** The collection and use of the new information must be reasonably necessary and proportionate to achieve the identified purpose(s) (\u00a7 7002(d)).\n*   **Consent Requirements:** If the collection or processing of the new information does not meet the requirements set forth in \u00a7 7002(a), the business must obtain the consumer\u2019s consent in accordance with \u00a7 7004 before collection (\u00a7 7002(e)).\n*   **Notice Requirements:** The new Notice at Collection must comply with the general requirements for such notices, including being made available at or before the point of collection (\u00a7 7012(c), (d)).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8916,
