  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7121_002",
    "query": "After the initial phased rollout concludes on April 1, 2030, what is the annual recurring timeframe and audit period for completing subsequent cybersecurity audit reports?",
    "target_section": "7121",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7121(b), after April 1, 2030, if a business meets section 7120 criteria on January 1 of a year for the preceding year, the business must complete a cybersecurity audit covering the next 12 calendar months, and file the audit report by April 1 of the following year (e.g., meeting criteria on Jan 1, 2035 requires an audit from Jan 1, 2035 to Jan 1, 2036, with report due April 1, 2036).",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, the recurring requirements for cybersecurity audits following the initial rollout period are as follows:\n\n### Recurring Audit Schedule\nAfter April 1, 2030, the schedule for subsequent audits is determined by the business\u2019s status as of January 1 of a given year (\u00a7 7121(b)):\n\n*   **Determination Date**: If, on January 1 of any year, a business meets the criteria set forth in section 7120 for the preceding year, it is required to complete a cybersecurity audit (\u00a7 7121(b)).\n*   **Audit Period**: The audit must cover the 12-month period immediately following that January 1 date (\u00a7 7121(b)).\n*   **Report Completion Deadline**: The business must complete its cybersecurity audit report by April 1 of the year following the audit period (\u00a7 7121(b)).\n\n**Example**: As provided in \u00a7 7121(b), if a business meets the criteria as of January 1, 2035, the audit covers the period from January 1, 2035, through January 1, 2036. The corresponding audit report must be completed by April 1, 2036.\n\n### Submission of Certification\nIn addition to the audit report, the business must submit a written certification to the California Privacy Protection Agency (CPPA) (\u00a7 7124(a)):\n\n*   **Submission Deadline**: The certification must be submitted no later than April 1 following the year the business was required to complete the audit (\u00a7 7124(b)).\n*   **Method**: The certification must be submitted via the Agency\u2019s website at https://cppa.ca.gov/ (\u00a7 7124(d)).\n\n*Note: While the provided text outlines the timing requirements for the audit report and the certification, it does not define the specific criteria for businesses required to conduct audits under \"section 7120,\" as that specific section is not included in the provided source material.*",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8418,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is legally precise, mirrors the ground truth perfectly, and provides additional helpful context regarding the certification process while correctly noting the limitations of the provided source material. It is accurate, well-structured, and avoids hallucinations.",
    "model_refusal": false,
    "execution_time_sec": 6.944,
    "retrieved_sources": [
      {
        "parent_id": "v2026_sec7121_parent_all",
        "section": "7121",
        "section_title": "Timing Requirements for Cybersecurity Audits and Audit Reports.",
        "rerank_score": 0.365,
        "snippet": "\u00a7 7121. Timing Requirements for Cybersecurity Audits and Audit Reports.\n(a)\nA business must complete its first cybersecurity audit report no later than:\n(1)\nApril 1, 2028, if the b..."
      },
      {
