    "eval_id": "eval_7157_003",
    "query": "Are full CCPA risk assessment reports submitted annually to the CPPA by default, and how quickly must a business produce them if demanded by regulators?",
    "target_section": "7157",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.5,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7157(e), businesses submit only summary information and attestations annually. Full risk assessment reports are not submitted routinely, but the CPPA or the California Attorney General may require a business to submit its full risk assessment reports at any time. Upon receiving such a request, the business MUST submit its full risk assessment reports within 30 calendar days.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the provided regulatory context, here are the requirements regarding the submission of risk assessments to the Agency:\n\n### **Annual Submission Requirements**\nBusinesses are **not** required to submit their full, detailed risk assessment reports to the Agency on an annual basis. Instead, they must submit specific summary information as outlined in **\u00a7 7157(b)**. \n\nThis summary submission must include:\n*   Business name and contact information (**\u00a7 7157(b)(1)**).\n*   The time period covered by the submission (**\u00a7 7157(b)(2)**).\n*   The total number of risk assessments conducted or updated, categorized by processing activity (**\u00a7 7157(b)(3)**).\n*   Confirmation of whether the processed data involved specific categories of personal or sensitive personal information defined in Civil Code section 1798.140 (**\u00a7 7157(b)(4)**).\n*   An attestation of compliance signed by a member of the executive management team meeting specific requirements (**\u00a7 7157(b)(5), \u00a7 7157(c)**).\n\n### **Submission Deadlines for Summary Information**\n*   **For 2026 and 2027**: The information must be submitted no later than **April 1, 2028** (**\u00a7 7157(a)(1)**).\n*   **After 2027**: The information must be submitted no later than **April 1** of the year following the year in which the risk assessments were conducted (**\u00a7 7157(a)(2)**).\n\n### **Production of Full Reports upon Demand**\nWhile the full report is not submitted automatically, the Agency or the Attorney General may request a business\u2019s full risk assessment reports at any time (**\u00a7 7157(e)**). \n\n*   **Timeframe for Compliance**: A business must submit the requested full risk assessment reports within **30 calendar days** of the Agency\u2019s or the Attorney General\u2019s request (**\u00a7 7157(e)**).\n\n***\n\n*Note: The provided context outlines the requirements for submitting risk assessment information and reports to the Agency, but it does not detail every internal documentation standard required for the full report itself beyond those listed in \u00a7 7152.*",
