    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7003(d), a mobile application must include a conspicuous link in its privacy policy accessible through the platform or download page, AND it must also be accessible through a link directly within the application itself, such as through the application's settings menu.",
    "generated_answer": "Under the updated requirements in \u00a7 7003, subsection (d), a mobile application must ensure that a conspicuous link is:\n\n1.  **Included in the business's privacy policy**, which itself must be accessible through the mobile application\u2019s platform page or download page.\n2.  **Accessible within the application itself**, specifically through the application\u2019s settings menu.\n\n**Amendment Context:**\nThe 2026 update to \u00a7 7003(d) refined the language regarding the in-app link. While the 2023 version stated the link \"may\" also be accessible through the settings menu, the updated 2026 rule makes this a mandatory requirement, stating it \"must\" also be accessible through a link within the application, such as through the settings menu. Additionally, \u00a7 7003(c) was updated to clarify that for websites, the link must be similar in manner to other links on *any* webpage where personal information is collected, rather than just the homepage.",
