    "ground_truth_answer": "No. Under \u00a7 7222(b)(4)(A), directing a consumer to the beginning of a general privacy policy so that they must scroll through other information does NOT satisfy the requirement. The business must provide a link that takes the consumer directly to the specific section of the privacy policy that contains instructions for exercising CCPA rights.",
    "generated_answer": "No, a business is not permitted to direct a consumer to the top of its general privacy policy to satisfy the instruction requirements for an ADMT access request.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7222(b)(4)(A)**, while a business may comply with the instruction requirements by providing a link to the specific section of the privacy policy that contains those instructions, the following restrictions apply:\n\n*   **Direct Link Required**: The link must take the consumer directly to the specific section of the privacy policy that contains the instructions.\n*   **Prohibition on Redirecting**: Directing the consumer to the beginning of the privacy policy (the \"top\") does not satisfy the requirement.\n*   **Prohibition on Burdensome Navigation**: The business may not direct the consumer to any section of the privacy policy that does not contain the instructions, as this would require the consumer to scroll through other information to find the relevant content.",
