    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7062(g), if a business has no reasonable method to verify consumers, it must explain why in its privacy policy. The business MUST evaluate and document whether a reasonable verification method can be established at least once every 12 months, in connection with its annual privacy policy update.",
    "generated_answer": "If a business determines that it has no reasonable method to verify the identity of a consumer to the degree of certainty required for specific data requests, it must evaluate and document whether a reasonable method can be established at least once every 12 months (\u00a7 7062(g)).\n\nThis requirement is tied to the business's obligation to update its privacy policy in accordance with Civil Code section 1798.130, subdivision (a)(5) (\u00a7 7062(g)). Furthermore, if a business lacks a reasonable method to verify any consumer, it must explain the reason for this absence within its privacy policy (\u00a7 7062(g)).",
