  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7001_011",
    "query": "Is a consumer's neural data (such as brain wave activity measured by a neurotech headset) considered sensitive personal information under California regulations?",
    "target_section": "7001",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.5,
    "key_term_recall": 0.6,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Yes. Under \u00a7 7001(bbb)(1)(G), sensitive personal information explicitly includes a consumer's neural data, defined as information generated by measuring the activity of a consumer's central or peripheral nervous system that is not inferred from nonneural information.",
    "generated_answer": "Yes, a consumer\u2019s neural data is considered sensitive personal information under California regulations.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7001(bbb)(1)(G)**, \"sensitive personal information\" includes a consumer\u2019s neural data, which is defined as:\n\n*   Information generated by measuring the activity of a consumer\u2019s central or peripheral nervous system; and\n*   Information that is not inferred from non-neural information.\n\nPlease note that per **\u00a7 7001(bbb)**, sensitive personal information does not include information that is defined as \u201cpublicly available\u201d under Civil Code section 1798.140, subdivision (v)(2).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9394,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is legally precise, fully aligned with the ground truth, and provides additional relevant context regarding the 'publicly available' exception, which enhances the completeness of the response without introducing hallucinations.",
    "model_refusal": false,
    "execution_time_sec": 6.059,
    "retrieved_sources": [
      {
        "parent_id": "v2026_sec7001_child_bbb",
        "section": "7001",
