  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7012_002",
    "query": "Can an online business satisfy Notice at Collection rules by providing a website link that redirects consumers to the very top of its general privacy policy?",
    "target_section": "7012",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.0,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "No. Under \u00a7 7012(f), providing a link to the privacy policy satisfies Notice at Collection ONLY IF the link takes the consumer directly to the specific section containing the required collection disclosures. Directing the consumer to the beginning of the privacy policy, requiring them to scroll through unrelated text, does not satisfy the legal standard.",
    "generated_answer": "No, an online business cannot satisfy the \"Notice at Collection\" requirements by redirecting a consumer to the top of its general privacy policy.\n\nAccording to **\u00a7 7012(f)**, if a business provides a link to its privacy policy to satisfy the Notice at Collection requirements, the link must take the consumer **directly to the specific section** of the privacy policy that contains the information required under subsections (e)(1) \u2013 (6).\n\nThe regulations explicitly state that:\n*   Directing a consumer to the **beginning** of the privacy policy is insufficient.\n*   Directing a consumer to another section of the privacy policy that does not contain the required information\u2014thereby forcing the consumer to scroll through unrelated information to find the relevant categories of information collected or whether the business sells/shares information\u2014**does not satisfy this standard** (**\u00a7 7012(f)**).\n\nTo be compliant, the link must provide immediate access to the specific disclosures required by **\u00a7 7012(e)**, which include:\n*   A list of categories of personal and sensitive personal information collected (**\u00a7 7012(e)(1)**).\n*   The purpose(s) for collection and use (**\u00a7 7012(e)(2)**).\n*   Whether that information is sold or shared (**\u00a7 7012(e)(3)**).\n*   Retention periods or criteria for determining retention periods (**\u00a7 7012(e)(4)**).\n*   A link to the Notice of Right to Opt-out of Sale/Sharing, if applicable (**\u00a7 7012(e)(5)**).\n*   A link to the business\u2019s privacy policy (**\u00a7 7012(e)(6)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.9047,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is legally precise, fully aligned with the ground truth, and provides additional helpful context regarding the specific requirements of \u00a7 7012(e) that must be accessible via the link. It correctly identifies the regulatory prohibition against linking to the top of a privacy policy.",
