  {
    "eval_id": "eval_7025_010",
    "query": "What privacy policy disclosures are mandatory for a business claiming exemption from posting 'Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information' links under frictionless processing rules?",
    "target_section": "7025",
    "expected_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "actual_route": "POLICY_LOOKUP",
    "route_correct": true,
    "route_reasoning": "Standard regulatory policy lookup targeting active 2026 regulations.",
    "answerable": true,
    "abstained": false,
    "section_hit": true,
    "hit_in_top_1": true,
    "precision_at_k": 0.3333,
    "key_term_recall": 0.25,
    "citation_valid": true,
    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7025(g)(2)(A)\u2013(D), the business must include in its privacy policy: (1) A description of the right to opt-out of sale/sharing; (2) An explicit statement that it processes opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner; (3) Instructions on how consumers can implement opt-out preference signals for frictionless processing; and (4) Instructions for any other available opt-out methods.",
    "generated_answer": "To qualify for the exemption from posting the \"Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\" link or the Alternative Opt-out Link by processing opt-out preference signals in a \"frictionless manner,\" a business must satisfy specific disclosure requirements within its privacy policy as outlined in **\u00a7 7025(g)(2)** and **\u00a7 7011(a)(3)**.\n\n### Mandatory Privacy Policy Disclosures\nUnder **\u00a7 7025(g)(2)**, the business must include the following information in its privacy policy:\n*   **Description of Rights**: A description of the consumer\u2019s right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of their personal information (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(A)**).\n*   **Statement of Frictionless Processing**: A statement that the business processes opt-out preference signals in a frictionless manner (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(B)**).\n*   **Implementation Instructions**: Information on how consumers can implement opt-out preference signals for the business to process in a frictionless manner (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(C)**).\n*   **Other Methods**: Instructions for any other method by which the consumer may submit a request to opt-out of sale/sharing (**\u00a7 7025(g)(2)(D)**).\n\n### Additional Required Explanations\nUnder **\u00a7 7011(a)(3)**, the privacy policy must also include:\n*   **Processing Explanation**: An explanation of how an opt-out preference signal will be processed, including whether the signal applies to the device, browser, consumer account, and/or offline sales, and under what circumstances (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(F)**).\n*   **Notice of Right to Opt-out**: If the business is required to provide a Notice of Right to Opt-out of Sale/Sharing, the privacy policy must contain the contents of that notice or a link to it in accordance with **\u00a7 7013(f)** (**\u00a7 7011(a)(3)(C)**).\n\n### Critical Compliance Caveat\nA business may only claim this exemption if it is able to **fully effectuate** the consumer's request to opt-out of sale or sharing via the opt-out preference signal (**\u00a7 7025(g)(3)**). \n\nIf a business engages in activities that require additional information to process an opt-out (such as offline sales that require a user to be logged into an account), it cannot claim the exemption because the opt-out preference signal alone is insufficient to cover those instances (**\u00a7 7025(g)(3)(A)**). Businesses that only sell or share information online for cross-context behavioral advertising are generally positioned to use this exemption, as the signal fully effectuates the request for those online activities (**\u00a7 7025(g)(3)(B)**).",
    "semantic_similarity": 0.8921,
    "llm_judge_score": 5.0,
    "llm_judge_reasoning": "The candidate answer is excellent. It fully captures all the requirements listed in the ground truth while providing additional, highly relevant regulatory context (\u00a7 7011(a)(3) and \u00a7 7025(g)(3)) that enhances the legal utility of the answer without introducing hallucinations. It is precise, well-structured, and demonstrates a superior understanding of the CCPA regulations regarding frictionless processing.",
    "model_refusal": false,
    "execution_time_sec": 7.172,
