    "ground_truth_answer": "Under \u00a7 7155(c), a business must retain its risk assessments (including original and updated versions) for as long as the processing activity continues OR for five (5) years after the completion of the risk assessment, whichever duration is later.",
    "generated_answer": "Based on the statutory comparative context provided, here is the analysis regarding the retention requirements for risk assessment reports:\n\n**1. Status of Retention Requirements**\nThe provided comparative context does not contain any provisions establishing a specific retention period for \"risk assessment reports.\" \n\n**2. Analysis of Statutory Evolution**\n*   **2023 Regulations:** The term \"Risk assessment report\" was not defined, and no retention requirements for such a document were provided in the text.\n*   **2026 Regulations:** The term \"Risk assessment report\" was introduced as a new definition under **\u00a7 7001(zz)**. This section defines the report as the document created by a business required to conduct a risk assessment, specifically incorporating the information set forth in **\u00a7 7152, subsections (a)(1)\u2013(3), (6)\u2013(9)**. \n\n**Conclusion**\nWhile the 2026 regulations formally define the \"Risk assessment report\" in **\u00a7 7001(zz)**, the provided text **does not contain any statutory language specifying how long a business must retain original or updated versions of these reports.** Consequently, there has been no change regarding retention periods because no such requirement exists within the provided comparative context for either the 2023 or 2026 regulations.",
