    "generated_answer": "To submit a request to opt-out of Automated Decisionmaking Technology (ADMT) on a consumer\u2019s behalf, an authorized agent must provide the following documentation to the business:\n\n*   **Signed Permission**: The agent must provide written permission signed by the consumer that demonstrates they have been authorized to act on the consumer\u2019s behalf (\u00a7 7221(j)).\n\n**Compliance Notes:**\n*   **Denial of Request**: A business is permitted to deny a request from an authorized agent if the agent fails to provide the required signed permission from the consumer (\u00a7 7221(j)).\n*   **Security and Usage**: While the provided context for \u00a7 7221(j) specifically addresses the requirement for signed permission, authorized agents are generally required to implement and maintain reasonable security procedures to protect consumer information and are prohibited from using the collected information for any purpose other than fulfilling the request, verification, or fraud prevention (\u00a7 7063(c)-(d)).",
